        "AbstractText": "Subcutaneous occipital nerve region stimulation is becoming an important part of the overall treatment regimen for a number of chronic headache syndromes refractory to nonsurgical, medical management. A combination of improved device technology and methodology, further understanding about appropriate indications and achievement of on-label FDA status should support continued use and success of this neuromodulation modality."
